cm: x=5 is sh's - var x 5 makes a variable, set x 5 changes one, set env[X] 5 the environment (line 1)
cm: $1 is sh's - the script's arguments are $args, $args[0] the first (line 1)
cm: for name values... { } - no in, as sh has (line 1)
cm: name() { } is sh's - def name { } makes a function (line 1)
cm: if condition { ... } - a block, not sh's then and fi (line 1)
cm: export is sh's - set env[NAME] value (line 1)
cm: local is sh's - var name value - a def's variables are its own (line 1)
cm: unset is sh's - del name[key], del env[NAME] (line 1)
cm: function is sh's - var name {|params| ... } (line 1)
cm: `...` is sh's - $( ) captures a command's output (line 1)
cm: fi is sh's - blocks: if cond { }, while cond { }, for x values { }, case v { } (line 1)
cm: nosuchprog: no such program (line 1)
still here
cm: echo -n and -e are sh's - echo prints its words and a newline; printf '%s' text prints none (line 1)
cm: @( ) is not taken in a double-quoted text or a here-document - $( ) is the text there, \@( the characters (line 1)
